      "summary": "Cardrona Alpine Resort is open for skiing today, with 5 cm of fresh overnight snow and snow showers expected to dissipate this morning, leaving a cloudy day ahead. There's been 5 cm of new snow in the past 24 hours, holding the natural base at 112 cm; it's currently -2°C with light winds around 6 km/h gusting to 11 km/h. Expect a little dust-on-crust in places this morning, with fresh snow sitting on variable conditions underneath, but still great turns to be had across the mountain. All 10 of 10 lifts are open, with 7 of 9 park features and all 10 of 10 terrain zones open. Main Basin and Valley View open from 8:30am, with Captains, Willows, Soho and the T-Bar following from 9am. She'll Be Right Community Day is on today, with McPark closed for the event; the National Alpine Points races run from 10am in Arcadia Valley into Powder Keg, closed to the public until racing wraps up mid-morning. Olympic Pipe closes at 12pm today. The access road is chain-free but chains must be carried, with an active road hazard advisory in place. Lifts & terrain Lifts Open 10 / 10 Runs Open 0 / 38 Percent open 0 %",
