      "summary": "Treble Cone is open for skiing today, with just three days left in the season and 5 cm of fresh snow overnight above the top of the Six Seater, tapering to a dusting at the base. Grooming has put the finishing touches on the on-piste terrain, which is skiing beautifully, though off-piste stays firm and dusty until things soften up; the natural base holds at 150 cm at the top of Home Basin. It's currently -1°C with light winds around 5 km/h gusting to 8 km/h, with cloudy periods and a chance of a morning shower, clearing to fine in the afternoon and winds turning northwesterly in the evening. All 3 of 3 lifts and all 11 of 11 groomed trails are open, with 7 of 9 terrain zones open. Home Basin runs 8:30am–4pm and Saddle Basin 9am–3:30pm today. The access road is chain-free but chains must always be carried, with an active road hazard advisory and a free shuttle running from the bottom of the access road. Tomorrow (Saturday) brings Kiri the Kea's birthday celebration on the mountain, with family fun, dress-ups and cake at noon for the final weekend of the season. Lifts & terrain Lifts Open 3 / 3 Runs Open 0 / 59 Percent open 0 %",
